- $ d_1 = 80 $ (km)
- $ d_2 = 150 $ (km)

Now, the question asks for the *difference* in the cost values of the two routes, assuming:

$$
\text{Cost} = \text{Distances} \times (\text{Rate per Unit Distance})
$$

Given only the **distances**, this becomes:

$$
\text{Difference in Cost} = |d_2 - d_1| = |150 - 80| = 70
$$

This is the **absolute change in cost** of taking the longer (150 km vs. 80 km) rather than the shorter route (80 km).

